---
// Privacy, from the README's "Privacy" (1.0). What changed from 0.2's page: meeting audio is written
// to disk, beside the library; the claim is "no telemetry of its own", with the Windows App SDK's
// part in Windows diagnostics stated; the network list is 1.0's (Hugging Face at pinned revisions,
// GitHub releases for updates, your own provider); every feature that sends text asks first, and
// Local only refuses remote endpoints in code.
import Shot from './Shot.astro';
import { APP_SDK_NOTE_URL, HUGGING_FACE_URL } from '../lib/constants';
---

<section class="section band-dark glow-quiet" id="privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="privacy-title" class="sr-only">Privacy</h2>
    <p class="statement">
      Your voice stays on your machine. <span>Text leaves only when a feature you switched on asks first, and you
      say where it goes.</span>
    </p>

    <dl class="specs">
      <div>
        <dt>Recognised here, never uploaded</dt>
        <dd>Audio is captured, transcribed and stored locally. No account, and no telemetry of its own.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>The library is a local file</dt>
        <dd>
          SQLite, with meetings’ audio beside it, written to disk as it records. Nothing syncs.
          <span class="paths"><code>~/Library/Application Support/Inkwell</code><code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Inkwell</code></span>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Local only is on unless you turn it off</dt>
        <dd>While it is on, the core refuses any language-model endpoint that is not on this machine, in code.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Every feature that sends text asks first</dt>
        <dd>Polish, voice edit, summaries and Ask each ask where your words will go, and ask again if that changes. Only text is sent, never audio.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <details class="more wide-open privacy-more">
      <summary>Keys, logs, the network and updates</summary>
      <div class="more-body">
        <dl class="specs">
      <div>
        <dt>Keys and logs</dt>
        <dd>Keys stay in the Keychain or the Credential Manager and go straight to your provider; no server of this project is in the path. Logs never contain what you said.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>What connects to the network</dt>
        <dd>
          Model downloads from <a href={HUGGING_FACE_URL}>Hugging Face</a> at pinned revisions, SHA-256 checked; update
          checks against the project’s GitHub releases; and your language-model provider, if you set one up.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Updates</dt>
        <dd>On the Mac, Sparkle asks before its first automatic check and sends no system profile. On Windows, Inkwell checks only when you press Check Now.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Windows App SDK</dt>
        <dd>
          Microsoft’s runtime in the Windows app takes part in Windows’ own diagnostic data (Settings > Privacy &
          security > Diagnostics & feedback). It never sees what you dictate or record. <a href={APP_SDK_NOTE_URL}>Details</a>.
        </dd>
      </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </details>
    <div class="privacy-shot">
      <Shot shot="p3" optional sizes="(min-width: 46rem) 30rem, 100vw" caption="Polish asks before its first send." />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
